t and its proof is acceptable. However, it is applied to \\(\\ell'\\) and \\(\\omega'\\) whose identification is already invalid. Thus the use of Lemma\u202f3 does not rescue the argument.\n\n#### Step\u202f13 \u2013 Equation (12) and final tangency argument\n- The step \u201cInversion preserves tangency\u201d is only true when the point of tangency is the centre of inversion. Here the tangency point is \\(B'\\neq A\\); therefore the claim that the pre\u2011image of a tangent circle is tangent to the pre\u2011image of the other circle is false. \u2192 **Critical Error**.\n\n#### Overall assessment\nThe solution hinges on several false geometric statements (midpoint of a chord, preservation of orthocentre, behaviour of inversion on parallel lines) and on an incorrect application of Lemma\u202f1. These constitute **Critical Errors** that break the logical chain early (step\u202f7). Consequently the proof does not establish the required result."
