io \\(\\frac{BE}{BF}=k\\) from Lemma\u202f2 and then applies the \u201csymmedian criterion\u201d. Because Lemma\u202f2 is false, the equality \\(\\frac{BE}{BF}=k\\) is not established, and the identification of \\(AP\\) as a symmedian lacks any valid foundation.\n\n**Issue Identified (Critical Error):** The conclusion rests on the invalid result of Lemma\u202f2; therefore Lemma\u202f3 is not proven.\n\n---\n\n### Lemma\u202f4 (orthocenter\u202f+\u202fsymmedian \u21d2 tangent)\n\n> \u201cIn any triangle the altitude from \\(X\\) is the isogonal conjugate of the median \\(XM\\).\u201d\n\n**Issue Identified (Critical Error):**  \nIn a general triangle, the altitude from a vertex is the isogonal conjugate of the **line through the vertex that is symmetric to the median with respect to the internal angle bisector**, not of the median itself. The median and the altitude are not isogonal unless the triangle is isosceles with the equal sides adjacent to the vertex. Hence the statement (7) derived from this claim is false in general, and the subsequent angle equalities (8)\u2013(9) do not follow. Consequently the proof that a line through the orthocenter parallel to the symmedian is tangent is unsupported.\n\n---\n\n### Final Proof\n\nThe final step combines Lemma\u202f3 (invalid) and Lemma\u202f4 (invalid) to claim the desired tangency. Since both lemmas contain critical errors, the final conclusion is not justified.\n\n---\n\n### Overall Assessment\nThe solution fails at two essential junctures:\n\n1. **Lemma\u202f2** incorrectly asserts that a spiral similarity centred at \\(B\\) leaves the line \\(AP\\) invariant.\n2. **Lemma\u202f4** misstates a fundamental property of isogonal conjugates, claiming the altitude is the isogonal of the median.\n\nBoth errors invalidate the subsequent reasoning, making the proof incomplete and incorrect. Hence the solution does not meet the rigorous standards required for an IMO\u2011level proof."
