ors. Since those premises are false, the final tangency statement is not proven.  \n\n---\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe solution contains a **critical logical flaw** in \u00a72 (incorrect claim that the spiral similarity sends the circumcenter of one circle to the circumcenter of its image, leading to the false collinearity \\(A,P,B\\)). This error invalidates the subsequent chain of reasoning that relies on that collinearity and on the derived isosceles triangle \\(AMN\\). In addition, several steps are insufficiently justified (missing angle\u2011preservation arguments, incomplete Simson\u2011line proof, unproved cyclicity claims). Because the core of the argument collapses, the solution does **not** constitute a valid proof of the problem statement."
