02f2).  \n2. Unproved uniqueness of a circle orthogonal to \\(\\Gamma\\) through \\(B\\) and \\(F\\) (Lemma\u202f2).  \n3. Unjustified claim that a spiral similarity maps orthocenters to orthocenters (Lemma\u202f5).  \n4. Faulty proof of the \u201cParallel\u2011through\u2011orthocentre Lemma\u201d (Lemma\u202f4).  \n5. Misidentification of the altitudes of \\(\\triangle ABF\\) with the perpendiculars from Lemma\u202f3 (Lemma\u202f5).\n\nBecause these errors occur early and are foundational for the later arguments, the logical chain of the proof is broken. Consequently, the solution does **not** constitute a valid proof of the problem statement."
