orted.\n\n* **Location:** Final comparison \u2013 \u201cLemma\u202f2 gives \\(\\angle BTA = \\angle BFA\\). Because \\(F\\) lies on the circle \\((BEF)\\), the angle \\(\\angle BFA\\) equals the angle subtended by the chord \\(BT\\) at the point \\(F\\) \u2026\u201d\n  * **Issue:** Critical Error \u2013 Lemma\u202f2 itself is based on the false parallelisms, so the equality \\(\\angle BTA = \\angle BFA\\) is not proven. Moreover, the statement that \\(\\angle BFA\\) equals the angle subtended by chord \\(BT\\) at \\(F\\) presumes \\(A\\) also lies on \\((BEF)\\), which is not true.\n\n---\n\n###"
