d by the chord\u2019s endpoints and the centre.\n\n* **Location:** Lemma\u202f2 proof \u2013 \u201cThe perpendicular bisector of \\(AD\\) passes through the centre \\(P\\) and therefore bisects the angle formed by the tangents to the circle at \\(A\\) and at \\(D\\).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** Critical Error \u2013 The statement that a line through the centre perpendicular to a chord bisects the angle between the two tangents at the chord\u2019s endpoints is false; the correct statement is that it bisects the *central* angle subtended by the chord, not the angle between tangents.\n\n* **Location:** \u201cBecause \\(C\\) lies on \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(D\\) is the image of \\(C\\) under the homothety \\(\\mathcal H_{A,k}\\), the rays \\(AC\\) and \\(AD\\) are symmetric with respect to the line \\(AB\\).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** Critical Error \u2013 Even if Lemma\u202f1 were correct, there is no reason for \\(AB\\) to be the axis of symmetry of the homothety; the homothety centred at \\(A\\) does **not** in general make \\(AC\\) and \\(AD\\) symmetric about \\(AB\\).\n\n* **Location:** \u201c\\(\\angle (BT,\\ell)=\\angle (BP,PA)=\\angle BPF\\)\u201d (step\u202f4.2).  \n  **Issue:** Critical Error \u2013 The equality \\(\\angle (BT,\\ell)=\\angle (BP,PA)\\) is asserted without justification; the relationship between the direction of \\(BT\\) and the direction of \\(BP\\) is not established, and the use of the orthocenter property \\(PH\\perp MN\\) is irrelevant to this angle.\n\n* **Location:** \u201cA homothety centred at \\(A\\) preserves oriented angles with vertex \\(A\\); consequently for any point \\(X\\) \\(\\angle XAE = \\angle XAF\\).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** Critical Error \u2013 A homothety does **not** preserve angles whose vertex is the centre of the homothety; it preserves *collinearity* and *ratios of distances*, but angles with vertex at the centre are unchanged only because the points lie on the same ray, not because of any general angle\u2011preserving property. The conclusion \\(\\angle BFT = \\angle BCF\\) is therefore unsupported.\n\n* **Location:** \u201c\\(\\angle (PA,PC)=0\\) because \\(PA=PC\\) and \\(AP\\) bisects the external angle at \\(A\\) (Lemma\u202f2).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** Critical Error \u2013 Equality of lengths \\(PA=PC\\) does **not** imply that the oriented angle \\(\\angle (PA,PC)\\) is zero; it only says that \\(P\\) lies on the perpendicular bisector of \\(AC\\). The claim that the angle is zero is unjustified.\n\n* **Location:** Overall \u201cReduction to a single angle equality\u201d section \u2013 the logical equivalence between tangency of \\(\\ell\\) and the angle equality \\(\\angle BPF=\\angle BCF\\) is derived from the flawed statements above, so the reduction itself is invalid.\n\n---\n\n##"
