mage of the circle \\((ACDP)\\) is the circle \\((AEFP)\\). Hence the four points \\(A,E,F,P\\) are concyclic. In particular\n\n\\[\n\\angle BFE=\\angle BAE. \\tag{2.6}\n\\]\n\n(The equality follows because \\(B\\) lies on both original circles \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\); after the similarity the chord \\(EF\\) corresponds to the chord \\(AC\\), and the inscribed angles subtended by these chords at the common point \\(B\\) are equal.)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.5  Tangency criterion\n\nLet \\(\\omega\\) be the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\). By the tangent\u2011chord theorem, a line through \\(B\\) is tangent to \\(\\omega\\) iff it makes with the chord \\(BE\\) (or \\(BF\\)) the same angle as the chord \\(EF\\) subtends at the opposite point of the circle:\n\n\\[\n\\ell\\text{ is tangent to }\\omega\\iff \\angle(\\ell,BE)=\\angle BFE. \\tag{2.7}\n\\]\n\nBecause of (2.5) the line \\(\\ell\\) is parallel to \\(PH_{MN}\\). From (2.4) the point \\(H_{MN}\\) lies on the circumcircle \\((PMN)\\); therefore the chord \\(BH_{MN}\\) of that circle subtends at the centre \\(P\\) the same angle as the chord \\(BF\\) subtends at the point \\(E\\) of \\(\\omega\\). Using (2.6) we obtain\n\n\\[\n\\angle(PH_{MN},BF)=\\angle BFE. \\tag{2.8}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\ell\\parallel PH_{MN}\\), (2.8) yields \\(\\angle(\\ell,BF)=\\angle BFE\\). The angles \\(\\angle(\\ell,BE)\\) and \\(\\angle(\\ell,BF)\\) are equal because the two lines \\(BE\\) and \\(BF\\) are symmetric with respect to the line \\(BA\\) which passes through the centre of the spiral similarity and therefore through the midpoint of the arc \\(EF\\) of \\(\\omega\\); equivalently, both are the angle between \\(\\ell\\) and the two sides of the triangle \\(BEF\\) issuing from the same vertex \\(B\\). Consequently\n\n\\[\n\\angle(\\ell,BE)=\\angle BFE,\n\\]\n\nwhich is exactly the condition (2.7). Hence \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to \\(\\omega\\) at \\(B\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.6  Conclusion\n\nThe line through the orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) satisfies the tangent\u2011chord condition for the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\); therefore it is tangent to that circle. This completes the proof. \u220e"
