arlier gaps, this step is not securely grounded.\n\n3. **Angle chase:** The proof combines (8), (9), and (10) to claim \\(\\angle(PH_{MN},BE)=\\angle BFE\\). Because (9) is false, the conclusion that \\(PH_{MN}\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(BEF\\) at \\(B\\) collapses.\n\n4. **Application of the tangent\u2011chord theorem:** Even if the angle equality held, the theorem requires the line to pass through the point of tangency (\\(B\\)). The proof never shows that \\(PH_{MN}\\) meets the circle \\((BEF)\\) at \\(B\\); it only shows an angle equality, which is insufficient.\n\n**Overall assessment of Lemma\u202f5:** The lemma contains a **critical error** (incorrect angle equality) and several justification gaps.\n\n---\n\n#### Final Assessment\n\nThe solution fails to provide rigorous justifications for key geometric relations:\n\n- The claim that \\(A,E,F,P\\) are concyclic with centre \\(P\\) is not proved correctly.\n- The perpendicularity \\(AP\\perp MN\\) is asserted without a valid argument.\n- The pivotal angle equality \\(\\angle BFE = \\angle BAE\\) is false, constituting a critical error that invalidates the final tangency argument.\n\nBecause the proof\u2019s logical chain is broken at a critical step, the solution cannot be considered correct."
