"**Final Verdict:** The solution contains a **Critical Error** that breaks the logical chain of the proof, rendering it invalid.\n\n**List of Findings:**\n* **Location:** \u201cThe left\u2011hand side is\u202f\u2220CPN (because\u202fC,P,N\u202fare collinear with\u202fN\u202fon the extension of\u202fPC) \u2026\u201d  \n  * **Issue:** **Critical Error** \u2013\u202fPoints\u202fC,\u202fP,\u202fN are **not collinear** in the given configuration; the statement that \u2220CPN is defined in this way is false, destroying the subsequent angle relations.\n* **Location:** \u201cSince\u202fPN\u202fis the perpendicular bisector of the chord\u202fAD\u202fof the circle\u202f(ACD) \u2026 consequently \u2220DPN = \u00bd\u2220DPA = \u2220DBA.\u201d  \n  * **Issue:** **Justification Gap** \u2013 The claim that\u202fPN\u202fis the perpendicular bisector of\u202fAD\u202fand that this yields the stated angle equality is not proved; it relies on the previous (invalid) collinearity claim.\n* **Location:** \u201cThe homothety\u202f\ud835\udcd7_A\u202fsends the whole circle\u202f\u03a9\u202fonto\u202f\u0393; it maps the chord\u202fAB\u202fof\u202f\u03a9\u202fonto the chord\u202fAB\u202fof\u202f\u0393.\u201d  \n  * **Issue:** **Justification Gap** \u2013 While a homothety centered at\u202fA\u202fdoes map one circle to the other, the argument that it maps chord\u202fAB\u202fto itself and therefore makes\u202fAB\u2225EF\u202fneeds a brief justification (the image of the line\u202fAE\u202fis\u202fAF, but the parallelism of\u202fAB\u202fand\u202fEF\u202fdoes not follow automatically).\n* **Location:** \u201cIn an isosceles trapezoid the base angles are equal, therefore \u2220EBA = \u2220ABF.\u201d  \n  * **Issue:** **Justification Gap** \u2013 The claim that\u202fABEF\u202fis an isosceles trapezoid (with\u202fAB\u2225EF\u202fand\u202fAE=AF) is not fully established; the equality of base angles follows only after confirming the trapezoid\u2019s properties.\n* **Location:** \u201cBy the tangent\u20