\n\nThis constitutes a **justification gap** (and in fact a factual error about lengths), but because the proof already failed earlier, it does not affect the overall verdict.\n\n---\n\n#### Step\u202f8 \u2013 From\u202fPH\u2225AB\u202fto tangency\nThis step combines the (invalid) angle relations from earlier with the (unjustified) properties of the quadrilateral\u202fABEF\u202fto claim tangency via the tangent\u2011chord theorem. Since the prerequisite angle equalities are not established, this step is also unsound.\n\n---\n\n#### Conclusion\nThe solution\u2019s core argument collapses at Step\u202f3 due to the false claim that points\u202fC,\u202fP,\u202fN\u202fare collinear, leading to an incorrect identification of angles and subsequent deductions. Additional gaps and inaccuracies appear later (steps\u202f7\u20138), but the critical error alone suffices to deem the solution invalid."
