ngency claim depends on:\n  1. Lemma\u202f5 (point \\(H\\) on \\((BEF)\\)) \u2013 invalid.\n  2. Lemma\u202f3 (line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) coincides with \\(PH\\)) \u2013 not proved.\n  3. Misinterpretation of the tangent\u2011chord theorem.\n\nBecause the foundational lemmas are either false or insufficiently justified, the tangency conclusion is unsupported.\n\n*Result:* **Critical Error** \u2013 The concluding statement is not derived from a valid chain of reasoning.\n\n---\n\n### Overall Assessment\n\nThe solution fails at its very first crucial step (Lemma\u202f1), where an incorrect symmetry argument leads to a false statement that \\(AP\\perp MN\\). All subsequent lemmas that rely on this fact inherit the error. Moreover, several later steps contain justification gaps (unproved standard facts, missing angle\u2011chase details) and a misapplication of the tangent\u2011chord theorem. Consequently the proof does not rigorously establish the required tangency, and the solution is **invalid**."
